{
  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "Prior Approval",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\r\rLocation Plan - D00\rProposed Block Plan - D09\rProposed First and Second Floor Plans - D02 Rev. C\rProposed Elevations Plan - D11 Rev. A\rProposed Streetscene Plan - D51 Rev. A\rRefuse Management Plan\rDaylight and Sunlight Assessment\rPlanning Statement\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until the enforcement measures safeguarding the car-free nature of the development have been put in place and evidence of these measure have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure the development is car-free as per paragraph 4 of Enfield DMD Policy 45.\r",
    "The development shall not be occupied until details of the required long-stay/short-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\tThese details should demonstrate:\r\tLocation: Near entrances or main access\r\tDesign: Stands\r\tSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit\r\tCoverage: Covered\r\tAccessibility: Step-free, no obstructions\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance ENV 08/162, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The development and future residents of the development will be exempt from obtaining parking permits for current and future controlled parking zones, unless they are a holder of a Blue Badge or any future equivalent. This will be secured by way of a Unilateral Undertaking, which is enforceable not only against the owner who signs the agreement but also future owners / occupants.\r\rReason: To mitigate car parking impacts to the setting\r"
  ],
